latest_news_url: https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=when:12h&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en

task (completed) {
  create a new command: /ai_news_podcast {
    - result: show top 5 result urls from {latest_news_url}
    - create a podcast button underneath the top 5 result urls:
      - when click on the button {
        - on top of the article, show a podcast icon {
          use 2 male voices, one act as a host and one act as guest 
          news_content: fetch the detail news content from {result}
          based on the {news_content}, draft a 2000 words article assuming it is a host/guest podcast, then read by the host and guest ai voice, use similar voice technology related to {directory_of_this_prompt}/news.prompt's task.news_voice_text_to_speech
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

Implemented:
app/chat_server.py
- Added the `/ai_news_podcast` command. It streams the top five stories from
the last 12 hours through news_fetch.php's Google News source. The prompt's
bare `when:12h` operator returns an empty Google News feed, so the command
keeps that 12-hour window and adds the word "news" to receive stories.
- Every news event for this command is tagged with `ai_news_podcast`, which
lets the browser add the podcast action only to this list.
- Added `POST /api/ai_news_podcast`. It accepts the five stories, fetches any
missing article bodies on demand, builds a bounded source block, and streams a
HOST/GUEST script from ornith-1.5:35b (approximately 2000 words, 5000-token
budget). The `start` event returns the two male TTS voices.
- `/api/tts` now accepts an optional `voice`; the cache key includes the voice.
`_podcast_voice_defaults()` picks `am_michael`/`am_adam` for Kokoro,
Daniel/Fred for macOS `say`, or `en-us+m3`/`en-us+m4` for espeak, with
PODCAST_HOST_VOICE and PODCAST_GUEST_VOICE overrides.
app/chat.html
- `/ai_news_podcast` renders its five links and adds a "Create podcast" button
underneath them.
- Clicking the button opens the top story and shows a microphone/podcast icon
at the top of the article. The icon drafts the script (streamed into the story
panel), then reads it aloud, alternating the host and guest male voices and
prefetching the next segment. Clicking it again stops playback or cancels a
script that is still being written.
- The podcast script is rendered as HOST/GUEST turns; a script without labels
is split into sentence groups so both voices are still used.

Verified:
- The command returns five Google News links and marks every event for the
podcast UI.
- The podcast endpoint streamed a 1,100+ word HOST/GUEST script for a test
story with the two Kokoro male voices in its start event.
- `/api/tts` returned distinct WAV audio for `am_michael` and `am_adam`.
- py_compile, node --check on the extracted front-end script, and php -l pass.
